  "prompt": "Fleur, in trade marketing, needs the readout of the checkout test AB-2025-01 for Monday's web shop meeting: for each variant, how many customers it had, how many of them converted, and how much revenue each of its customers brought. Leave out every customer assigned to both variants. A customer converted when the customer has a conversion in the test at or after the customer's assigned_at: a conversion before it does not count, and a customer who converted more than once counts once. Return one row for each variant, including a variant with no conversions. Return five columns, in this order: variant; n_customers; n_converted; conversion_rate_pct, 100 times n_converted divided by n_customers, rounded to 2 decimals; and revenue_per_customer_eur, the revenue_eur of the conversions that count, added up and divided by n_customers, in euros rounded to 2 decimals. A missing revenue_eur adds nothing, and a variant with no conversions that count gets 0. Sort by variant, alphabetically.",
